{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028695-a-difference-between-chronicles-of-darkness-and-classic-world-of-darkness","id":1028695,"title":"A difference between Chronicles of Darkness and classic World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-08T14:42:16-08:00","id":1028695,"title":"A difference between Chronicles of Darkness and classic World of Darkness","content":"I've noticed that in CoD, things tend to be a lot more mysterious and left to the Storyteller's discretion, whereas in classic WoD, there a lot more secrets revealed and cut-and-dried information given (even if it is only given to the ST). This is starting to change with Dark Eras, but I think it's still true overall. What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T15:10:32-08:00","id":1028706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028695-a-difference-between-chronicles-of-darkness-and-classic-world-of-darkness#post1028695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you've chosen a poor title for the thread that implies this is yet another 'which is better' and 'why do you think this is better than that.'<br /> <br /> Also while Dark Eras may have revealed secrets, it has actually expanded upon existing mysteries. Very little 'cut and dried' information has been that revelatory. The existence of Pangaea was basically a given. Things like the Underworld having been an ocean that drained away, or the Watchtowers being smaller imply other mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-08-2017, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T16:17:04-08:00","id":1028737,"title":"","content":"Yep, Chronicles leaves things mysterious. I like it that way a lot. My roommate disagrees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T16:29:20-08:00","id":1028747,"title":"","content":"There's also a lot of variation between the individual game lines. Mummy is far more &quot;cut and dried&quot; in ST-oriented material in the CofD than it is in the WoD (though part of that is that there's two essential versions of Mummy in the WoD and was never a full game line).<br /> <br /> The WoD can be frustratingly difficult to tease out what's supposed to be cut and dried, and what's unreliable narrator who thinks something is cut and dried. The CofD being more adamant about not locking anything too solidly into being the only way of doing things from the player/ST perspective helps put such things in context more easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T16:55:55-08:00","id":1028762,"title":"","content":"My go-to summary tends to be that the titular Darkness in the World of Darkness is a darkness of tone, whereas the Darkness in the Chronicles of Darkness is a darkness of opacity. The World of Darkness expresses its character through the exaggerated state of the world: rampant crime and disappearances, a maltheistic cosmology, and harsh injustices to the characters dwelling within. The Chronicles of Darkness express their character through the proliferation of mystery: communities are more geographically isolated, conditions are foggier, and there's strange things lurking at the corners that even the other strange lurking things can't piece together.<br /> <br /> It's not to say that either setting has a monopoly on those qualities. The World of Darkness has strange things that exist outside the context of the primary cosmologies of the gamelines, and the Chronicles of Darkness occasionally take on an oppressive, maltheistic tone. But they specialize differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:17:36-08:00","id":1028779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028695-a-difference-between-chronicles-of-darkness-and-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1028762#post1028762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My go-to summary tends to be that the titular Darkness in the World of Darkness is a darkness of tone, whereas the Darkness in the Chronicles of Darkness is a darkness of opacity. The World of Darkness expresses its character through the exaggerated state of the world: rampant crime and disappearances, a maltheistic cosmology, and harsh injustices to the characters dwelling within. The Chronicles of Darkness express their character through the proliferation of mystery: communities are more geographically isolated, conditions are foggier, and there's strange things lurking at the corners that even the other strange lurking things can't piece together.<br /> <br /> It's not to say that either setting has a monopoly on those qualities. The World of Darkness has strange things that exist outside the context of the primary cosmologies of the gamelines, and the Chronicles of Darkness occasionally take on an oppressive, maltheistic tone. But they specialize differently.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That has got to be the best and most eloquent description of differences between the two setting that I've ever heard. I take my hat off to you. *bows*<br /> <br /> As for which I prefer, well Julian it should come as no surprise at this point that I'm opacity all the way. Part of this is due to some bad experiences I had, but specifically between OWoD and CofD it all boils down to the maltheistic cosmos from OWoD and what I like to call the Warhammer Effect. If the world is already crap with no hope of improvement because &quot;Gehenna/Wyrm/Concensus/Ect&quot; then it create a sort of &quot;what's the point&quot; attitude within myself. While the all encompassing unknown promises nothing but uncertainty, which is considerably better than the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T18:20:21-08:00","id":1028810,"title":"","content":"Interesting, I got the Warhammer effect more from CofD, specifically from Requiem and Awakening. What's the point of accumulating power and connections? The Torpor will take it away. What's the point of fighting the Seers? The Exarchs already won. Ascension, IMO is much brighter than Awakening.<br /> <br /> Yes, WoD has it's big conflicts and looming apocalypse scenarios, but it always had the possibility of &quot;saving the world&quot; at the end (and you don't have to run for those scenarios). Even the last fight of the Garou wasn't inevitably doomed.<br /> <br /> Also, I could agree that CofD doesn't as &quot;cut and dry&quot;. If you don't have worldwide organizations and records, let alone persons who remember things, it naturally becomes murkier. Or, like in the case of VII, for example, it intentionally gives you different &quot;truths&quot;. That's the sandbox approach, it's good if you want to build your own world. In Masquerade, you get a book about the Tal'Mahe'ra, which, while certainly has unexplained parts and mysteries in it, it describes the faction in detail and what is it. It is good if you want ongoing story and for example novel lines (because you could build on the previous products' lore) or want to bring the worldwide fandom together (because it provides common ground).<br /> <br /> Basically, with CofD you have more tools and bigger freedom (and consequently less fear from lore-lawyers) to play with them, while in WoD you have a &quot;traditional&quot; rpg setting, with detailed history (although the unreliable narrator part is <i>very</i> important), events and definitive writings of the organizations, splats, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T18:38:20-08:00","id":1028819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028695-a-difference-between-chronicles-of-darkness-and-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1028810#post1028810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the point of accumulating power and connections? The Torpor will take it away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to find an answer to that is literally the whole point of the game :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's the point of fighting the Seers? The Exarchs already won. Ascension, IMO is much brighter than Awakening. </div> </div> </div>To me that's like asking &quot;What's the point in trying to cut down carbon emissions? Climate change has already started&quot;. Yes, Exarchs won, doesn't mean you should let their non-godly minions butcher innocents for amusement and turn anyone they desire into slaves. Also, you can eventually fight the Exarchs properly once you ascend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, WoD has it's big conflicts and looming apocalypse scenarios, but it always had the possibility of &quot;saving the world&quot; at the end (and you don't have to run for those scenarios). Even the last fight of the Garou wasn't inevitably doomed. </div> </div> </div>Nothing stops people from saving the world in CofD.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T18:45:03-08:00","id":1028821,"title":"","content":"I would disagree with the Warhammer effect at least in Requiem. The way I see it, there's even MORE purpose in accumulating power and connections in a Vampire game than in, say, a Mortals game / in real life. Mortals die, and don't get to reap the rewards after that point. You accumulate power to enjoy NOW, or to hand off to the descendents of your choice. Vampires can (attempt to) set up systems such that their power and connections will still remain when they wake up from torpor again, and not only enjoy power NOW, but ALSO enjoy it in the future (especially if they set up the proper systems to protect it while they're gone).<br /> As for Awakening, it depends on how active you play the Exarchs. If the Exarchs are a constant crushing force on the Pentacle, yeah, very much a Warhammer effect, they've already won and there's no way to beat them (or is there? dun dun dun...). If you play them as only occasionally interested in crushing the Pentacle, then you can very much have meaningful victories, just on a smaller scale. Think more &quot;We've blown up the Death Star! The Rebellion is saved!&quot;, less &quot;We've killed the Emperor and the rest of the Empire has just rolled over&quot;, and then you have a framework for removing (most) of the Warhammer Effect from Awakening. It definitely does suffer from the issue that the Bad Guys have practically irrevocably 'won' in the biggest possible picture, forcing you to focus on smaller-picture victories.<br /> <br /> edit: generally on the idea of vagueness, OP is totally correct. There 1 major exception I can think of; Mummy: the Curse relies on a very specific mythology and history, the discovery of which is part of the game experience. Otherwise, they've tried to design as many ST inspirations as they could. Many points in the mythology are meant to make you read them and go &quot;Ooooh, I want to play a Chronicle where the players discover the truth behind that! It would be cool if VII were ABC, which would mean they would be allied with the Nameless who could be XYZ and against the Strix who are alphabetagamma&quot; etc etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","user":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","date":". 01-08-2017, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T19:05:05-08:00","id":1028826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028695-a-difference-between-chronicles-of-darkness-and-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1028819#post1028819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to find an answer to that is literally the whole point of the game :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and that's part of why I never got as hooked on it as other people here. To me, powerful elders are a staple of the vampiric theme. I know, I know, there could be elders in Requiem, but still, the default &quot;cleaning the slate white at every couple hundred years at best&quot; thing was just not for my taste.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me that's like asking &quot;What's the point in trying to cut down carbon emissions? Climate change has already started&quot;. Yes, Exarchs won, doesn't mean you should let their non-godly minions butcher innocents for amusement and turn anyone they desire into slaves. Also, you can eventually fight the Exarchs properly once you ascend. </div> </div> </div>Oh, but that's exactly the same with the Technocracy in Ascension. The difference is: the Technos don't have omnipotent evil gods on their side and you don't have to earn a different state of being (which may or may not be attainable at all) to make even large scale differences. In Ascension, the two sides are waging the War, when in Awakening you're a fugitive of a lost war. In some sense Revised Ascension was more close to that (or rather, everyone lost there) and it certainly had a bleak romanticism to it, but it's not my preferred approach, I like the M20's New Millenium one much more. I might add that's one of my fears about how WWP will handle WoD, I fear they'll make it too hopeless and bleak and consequently, pointless to me, but we'll see. I hope they won't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing stops people from saving the world in CofD. </div> </div> </div>You missed the point. It came up that the WoD has &quot;no hope&quot; and I said it's not true and even the end-of-the-world scenarios aren't set in stone. I might add, I never really liked the apocalypses. I especially liked the idea of a smaller scale, cyclical Gehenna, for example, when it came up during the discussion when OP started to develop the new edition of Masquerade. I don't need inevitable apocalypses for WoD to keep it Dark.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T19:15:52-08:00","id":1028831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028695-a-difference-between-chronicles-of-darkness-and-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1028821#post1028821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would disagree with the Warhammer effect at least in Requiem. The way I see it, there's even MORE purpose in accumulating power and connections in a Vampire game than in, say, a Mortals game / in real life. Mortals die, and don't get to reap the rewards after that point. You accumulate power to enjoy NOW, or to hand off to the descendents of your choice. Vampires can (attempt to) set up systems such that their power and connections will still remain when they wake up from torpor again, and not only enjoy power NOW, but ALSO enjoy it in the future (especially if they set up the proper systems to protect it while they're gone).<br /> As for Awakening, it depends on how active you play the Exarchs. If the Exarchs are a constant crushing force on the Pentacle, yeah, very much a Warhammer effect, they've already won and there's no way to beat them (or is there? dun dun dun...). If you play them as only occasionally interested in crushing the Pentacle, then you can very much have meaningful victories, just on a smaller scale. Think more &quot;We've blown up the Death Star! The Rebellion is saved!&quot;, less &quot;We've killed the Emperor and the rest of the Empire has just rolled over&quot;, and then you have a framework for removing (most) of the Warhammer Effect from Awakening. It definitely does suffer from the issue that the Bad Guys have practically irrevocably 'won' in the biggest possible picture, forcing you to focus on smaller-picture victories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points, you could certainly do all of that to work around my &quot;problems&quot; (not really problems, just parts I don't like as much) and they could be very good and interesting elements of the game and story. However I feel they are indeed workarounds, not the default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> edit: generally on the idea of vagueness, OP is totally correct. There 1 major exception I can think of; Mummy: the Curse relies on a very specific mythology and history, the discovery of which is part of the game experience. Otherwise, they've tried to design as many ST inspirations as they could. Many points in the mythology are meant to make you read them and go &quot;Ooooh, I want to play a Chronicle where the players discover the truth behind that! It would be cool if VII were ABC, which would mean they would be allied with the Nameless who could be XYZ and against the Strix who are alphabetagamma&quot; etc etc </div> </div> </div>Yup, agree. CofD gives you a lot of possible pieces and options to build your own unique world, history, secrets and so on. WoD gives you a detailed, cohesive setting. Both are good for different purposes and reasons and I could appreciate all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T19:28:22-08:00","id":1028835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028695-a-difference-between-chronicles-of-darkness-and-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1028826#post1028826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, and that's part of why I never got as hooked on it as other people here. To me, powerful elders are a staple of the vampiric theme. I know, I know, there could be elders in Requiem, but still, the default &quot;cleaning the slate white at every couple hundred years at best&quot; thing was just not for my taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elders are powerful in Requiem.... When a elder comes out of torpor they don't lose their massive attributes or their disciplines or their devotions, and the next Requiem book to come out specifically has things like powerful devotions that elders have made over the centuries. They lose blood potency but other than that, elders are immensely powerful. Not sure what you're referring to with &quot;cleaning the slate&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, but that's exactly the same with the Technocracy in Ascension. </div> </div> </div>Both factions being villainous don't really make them &quot;exactly the same&quot; in my opinion....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> in Awakening you're a fugitive of a lost war. </div> </div> </div>Can't say I've seen anything like that suggested before in Awakening, either by fans or by the game itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 01-08-2017, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T21:06:59-08:00","id":1028857,"title":"","content":"Are we forgetting that Torpor doesn't <i>do that </i>any more in second edition? You don't lose your memories, you don't even lose your Attribute and Skill dots in excess of 5 if your Blood Potency drops. The only thing you lose is Vitae storage capacity, Vitae per turn, and bonus physical dice in Frenzy. And that's a temporary loss, accompanied by less restricted feeding until you get your Blood Potency back up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-09-2017, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T21:13:17-08:00","id":1028859,"title":"","content":"I'll jump in to point out the VtR 2e has very much downplayed the &quot;go into torpor and lose everything&quot; effect that 1e had. It still happens, but it isn't as bad, and there's a much stronger narrative on why vampires care about it (and working to compensate for it) than just losing power/etc. due to time. In 2e the biggest issue with torpor is losing Touchstones which far more personal than things like your contacts drying up. The hoary old elders that can maintain themselves despite the centuries are scary because of things like turning institutions into Touchstones instead of individual people that lets them stay connected despite torpor, and gives them a vest interest in ruthlessly ensuring those things withstand the test of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T23:31:46-08:00","id":1028896,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6363_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6363\" data-vbnamecard=\"6363\">PM\u00e1rk</a>, you make some excellent points. Although Requiem 2nd Edition has made Torpor less severe and Elders more prevalent and powerful, your points about the Warhammer effect still rings true for many aspects of both Requiem and the CofD. Also, I couldn't agree more about the doomsayer undertone in WoD and see cyclical Gehennas that are just part of Vampiric nature far more engaging and rewarding. (Because after all, every vampire fears the night their creator returns to take away everything again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> The only real comment I see fault with is the idea that the Ascension War in Awakening is a) hopeless and b) unaffected by the Mages of the Fallen World. <br /> <br /> For point a) the Exarchs aren't all powerful beings. Atlantis might not have even existed as the Diamond and Seers claim it did. The Exarchs may just be the representation for how the Ten Arcana try to dominate each other and the Fallen World. But they aren't able to smite anyone from on high without effectively opening themselves up from a dogpile of retribution from the Oracles, other Exarchs, Archmages, Old Gods, and all the other players in the Ascensions War. I can see why you would think that though, because for me the Sect war from Masquerade seems incredibly monolithic and all consuming. It seems to do little but keep the pecking order under the elders and there's little hope to ever make a meaningful difference when elder beings who might as well be gods can make a phone call and have you mortal family's house get swallowed up by the earth. Hell, the way the Seers are structured it might as well be designed by Methuselahs...OH MY GOD! :O<br /> <br /> For point b) in order for the Exarchs, or any player in the Ascension War for that matter, to be able to influence the Fallen World or Supernal Realms at all they must have two things: they need symbolic resonance which concepts from the Fallen World, and they need Quintessence from the physical world. Without it, they are Methuselahs without influence, herd, domain, or concept about how the world operates now surrounded by hungry sycophants who do. The secret truth is that the Exarchs NEED the Fallen World to survive. Without it they are nothing. Which means they are beholden to the ones who serve them, which is something they must never be allowed to know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 01-09-2017, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T12:53:42-08:00","id":1029713,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> , I didn't forget that 2e curbed back the torpor thin and I'm happy it did, the 1e version just felt wrong to me, because, as I wrote powerful elders spinning their webs for centuries and even millennia is just essential for the vampiric theme to me. Honestly, I'm very eager to see the upcoming elder book, it might be a great material even for Masquerade, as Damnation city was.<br /> <br /> However, the torpor was like the 1e version during the full run of 1e, as far as I'm aware and that was like that for a long time before 2e came out. Sorry, old habits and established initial impressions take time to change. For instance I could understand people who still have gripes about certain WoD elements, because they were less... refined at their first appearances.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> , those are interesting points about Awakening, thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-10-2017, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T14:25:02-08:00","id":1029755,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that WoD had an overall tone of \u201cthe end is near!\u201d Vampire had Gehenna, Werewolf had the Apocalypse. Wraith and Changeling didn't have specified end points per se; but both featured a seige mentality driven by the sense that the forces of Oblivion and Banality were eating away at the Underworld and the Dreaming, and that it wouldn't be long until they won. The latter-day gamelines (Hunter, Mummy, and Demon) were explicitly part of a world-ending metaplot. <br /> <br /> Mage was mostly an exception to this \u2014 although it should be noted that 2e featured the fall of the Traditions' strongholds and a Nephandic poisoning of the Technocracy, and that's before MRev introduced its \u201cAvatar Storm\u201d and \u201cthe Ascension War is over\u201d developments. <br /> <br /> With the X20 lines, that sense that the world is collapsing has largely gone away. But the type of Darkness that the WoD features is still one that emphasizes widespread corruption and evil. As always, M20 is the exception to this; though even here, the best indications we have of the author's preferred approach are that the Technocracy is all but Fallen, and that the Fallen have all but won.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T14:59:33-08:00","id":1029776,"title":"","content":"Wraith had Doomsday and Changeling had Long Winter, and those points totally exist as inevitabilites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:01:35-08:00","id":1029781,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'm not a big fan of the &quot;oh, WoD is sooooo '90s!&quot; opinion, but one thing (aside from the over-representation of Eastern martial arts) which I see as a pretty much '90ism is the whole THE END IS NEEEEAAAAR! thing. I was born at the very end of the '80s, and were a teen at the 2000's and in my twenties during the 2010's. I never accentuated the end of the world angle of WoD. I like Gehenna as a cyclical thing. I like the war against the Wyrm as a theme and the notion that the Garou and Fera are loosing and desperate, but for me the final battle tomorrow is unnecessary to enjoy the setting. Same with Mage, I like the concept of a constantly shifting reality and a never really ending ascension war. The wholesale infiltration of the Technocracy by Nephandi is too much for me, although some infiltration, even in the upper echelons I feel are great and thematic plot points.<br /> <br /> I especially don't like the end is nigh thing, because it has a built-in premise of actually ending it somewhere along the line and that's already &quot;killed&quot; WoD once. So I love the WoD setting, but don't really like the apocalypses angle. That's a big part of why I have an overwhelmingly good opinion on M20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T21:46:56-08:00","id":1029911,"title":"","content":"However, you need to consider the Apocalyptic tone to understand where the original World of Darkness came from. As I said, the X20 lines have moved away from it; but the nature of Darkness came from there. So even without it, you're still left with an overall sense that cWoD Darkness is corruption. Even in the X20 lines, there's a sense that the world is as bad or worse today than it was yesterday; the main change is that the end has been put off, perhaps indefinitely. It's no longer the Final Nights; but things are still bad and getting worse. <br /> <br /> I don't know how they're going to address this difference once they get around to the latter-day games; as I said, Hunter, Mummy, and Demon were all built around the Last Days metaplot and cannot easily be separated from it. All have the notion that a threshold has been crossed, and that unprecedented things are happening: Hunter is built on the notion that <s>angels</s> Messengers, Heralds, and Ministers were jolted out of complacency by the Week of Nightmares and have taken it upon themselves to raise an army to combat the monsters; Mummy: the Resurrection transformed the nature of its protagonists into champions of balance in a world where the Ghost Storm has destroyed balance; and Demon's premise is that the Ghost Storm cracked open the prison walls of the Abyss, flooding the world with literal demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T22:19:05-08:00","id":1029918,"title":"","content":"For me, personally, the sense of apocalypse is the main defining feature of the game. It's pretty much everything in that game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T22:24:50-08:00","id":1029921,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm curious how they'd handle it too. I hope they won't just curb back time to &quot;just before the end of the world&quot;, because that would cause the same long-term problems the original line had at the end. You just can't threatening with the apocalypse indefinitely. That's why I like the cyclical Gehenna and the New Millennium metaplot.<br /> <br /> I understand how the WoD was the product of the zeitgeist then and how the end of the century/millennium related fears were an important part of it. I just never particularly liked that angle, because again, it has the built-in premise of an actual ending. Think of Buffy. After a point it's an ongoing joke. However, I agree, that without it, the WoD still has a strong thematic anchor with corruption. You don't need to blow up Gotham in the end to have it.<br /> <br /> I admit, I never really delved deep into Mummy, Hunter and Demon, so i don't know how those lines are incompatible with the notion of an end-less WoD, but from the information gathered along the years I think it's manageable. Like, the Abyss cracked and the Demons came because of certain events. Okay, so, they're here for a time. Now what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T22:26:40-08:00","id":1029922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028695-a-difference-between-chronicles-of-darkness-and-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1029918#post1029918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, personally, the sense of apocalypse is the main defining feature of the game. It's pretty much everything in that game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different people, different tastes and focuses. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> To me WoD is about a bajilion things and the End is not even among the top 20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T22:40:16-08:00","id":1029927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028695-a-difference-between-chronicles-of-darkness-and-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1029922#post1029922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Different people, different tastes and focuses. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> To me WoD is about a bajilion things and the End is not even among the top 20.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that, and even a big part of why ChroD wins out over WoD is the fact Chronicles is legitimately more about cycles where World is legitimately about the End.<br /> <br /> I love the general Fuck It All Because We're Fucked nature of World-it's hard edged and visceral, and it does anti-aspirational characters in and stories in a way that's really cathartic-but there's a greater nuance and depth in Chronicles because it's not the end of the world, but rather, this is the way things are. It's not racing towards anything, not violently spiralling out of control-it's quieter, more thoughtful, perhaps more depressed, but also more hopeful too, and really more just about life. And while I do love me some punk-ass games where I'm going over 200 mph and there's a big wall sharing my grin as I race for it, Chronicles is a game that is not only going to be fun, but actually makes me believe I'll come out better having played it too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T23:15:41-08:00","id":1029935,"title":"","content":"Might be the reason why I never got as much from CofD as people like you. 'Cause WoD never was about the apocalypse for me, but about the darkness in people, the yes, how we're ruining the planet, each other and ourselves, not because the World's ending, but because we're horrible or just don't care. The conspiracies and hidden history and secret wars ere a big part too and so on. CofD never really did the &quot;<i>finally </i>there's no apocalypse looming over our head&quot; thing to me, because it never was an overwhelmingly important part in the first place in my eyes.<br /> <br /> My opinion is that Dark Ages works without an apocalypse. Wild West and Victorian too. Arguably Mage in every instance too. The other lines could work perfectly without it. Heck, I'm recently in the process of learning Shadowrun, since our group and ST wanted to play that and it felt very familiar to me after WoD, just everything turned into eleven and into the future and with out in the open supernatural elements (I'm still finding a dragon going for presidency and another being the head of the world's biggest megacorp hilarious <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). But the overall feeling is very close to how I always looked at WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}